<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George the Pious</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1484–1543</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as George, Margrave of Brandenburg-Ansbach</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George the Pious was Margrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-ansbach">Brandenburg-Ansbach</a> from 1515 to 1543, a member of the Franconian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollerns</a>. An early supporter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>, he introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> in his lands in 1528 and signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg-confession">Augsburg Confession</a> in 1530. He also acquired the Silesian duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krnov">Jägerndorf</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-the-pious.jpg" alt="George the Pious" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Krell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georg_der_Fromme_von_Brandenburg,_1539.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
